Short:        Doom 3 for AmigaOS 3 on PiStorm (Pi 4/3, ogles2)
Author:       R-Typer, Ladislawv
Type:         game/shoot
Version:      @VERSION@
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0
Requires:     PiStorm with Raspberry Pi 4 (or 3), Emu68, RTG, Doom 3 1.3.1 data
Distribution: GPLv3 (game code); Doom 3's data not included

Doom 3 (id Software, 2004) running natively on a 68k Amiga with a PiStorm.
The game code runs on Emu68, the graphics are drawn by the Raspberry Pi's
VideoCore GPU through ogles2.library 1.4 beta 2 (OpenGL ES 2.0 for AmigaOS 3, for
the Pi 4 and the Pi 3, included). Tested on a Pi 4; not yet tried on a Pi 3.
Based on dhewm3/d3es, the GPL release of Doom 3's source. Ported by R-Typer
and Ladislawv.

About 17 frames a second in Doom 3's own benchmark at 1920x1080 with the
Low settings; Low, Medium, High and Ultra settings, Paula or AHI sound, any
32-bit RTG screen size. Starts at 1280x720 with the frame rate shown; the
settings changed in the game's menus are kept.

New in 1.0-beta2: ogles2.library 1.4 beta 2, used from the game's own
drawer over one in LIBS:; demos read into memory before they play (the
timedemo shows the real speed: about 28 frames a second at 1280x720 Low);
a message instead of a crash without game data; shadows off at every
quality.

New in 1.0-beta1: the settings saved and used at every start, 1280x720 by
default, the game's speed following the frame rate, the precompressed
textures at every quality, only the screen sizes your system has in the
menu, the in-game screens taking clicks, colour icons, ogles2.library 1.4
with the Raspberry Pi 3.

You need your own copy of Doom 3: the nine pak00?.pk4 files of version
1.3.1 (GOG.com, Steam, or a boxed copy with the 1.3.1 patch). The BFG
Edition does not work. The free 2004 demo's data works too.

Unpack, copy the game's pk4 files into Doom3/base/, double-click Doom3.
Everything else is in the ReadMe inside the archive.

Source code: @SOURCE@
